  "reasoning": "The input molecule is a pinacol boronate ester featuring a 2-(cyclopropanecarboxamido)phenyl group attached to the boron center. The specified reaction type is Functional Group Interconversion (FGI). In organoboron methodology, FGI most commonly describes the reversible interconversion between a boronic ester and its parent boronic acid. Retrosynthetically, the cyclic pinacol chelate is removed and replaced with the two hydroxyl groups native to a boronic acid (rendered as B(O)O). This yields the corresponding arylboronic acid as the direct structural precursor. The forward transformation would correspond to the condensation of this boronic acid with pinacol under dehydrating conditions to afford the observed boronic ester.",
  "final_answer": "c2cccc(C(=O)NC3CC3)c2B(O)O"
}

